. " [:a {:href "/athletes/64548"} "Michele Mason-Brown"] " (AUS) finished second in Tokyo with 1.80 (5-10¾), but Balaş would clear that height, and then 1.82 (5-11½), 1.86 (6-1¼), and 1.90 (6-2¾) metres to win the gold medal. Two weeks after the Tokyo Olympics, Mason-Brown would become the second woman to jump over six feet."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "173"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75095"} "Iolanda Balaș"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "1.70 (=1)"] [:td {} "1.90 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/64548"} "Michele Mason-Brown"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1.70 (=1)"] [:td {} "1.80 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "205"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77175"} "Taisiya Chenchik"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "1.70 (10)"] [:td {} "1.78 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "22"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/65502"} "Aída dos Santos"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BRA"} 